# Shared .env for the six dev/staging/prod x local-storage/external-storage commands.
# Run from the repo root: Node.js 24+, pinned Yarn, Docker with Compose.
# Kubernetes is optional and has separate .env.kubernetes-local.example and
# .env.production.example templates. Kubernetes variables are not required here.
#
# SETUP: copy to <repo>/.env ONLY if it does not exist; otherwise merge settings.
# Everything is commented deliberately: uncomment only the values you use,
# replace sample credentials, and do not put inline comments on assignment lines.
# Keep .env private/out of Git. Never overwrite keys for a retained installation.
# Values are literal, not variable references; matching single/double quotes work.
# Set RIVET_ENV_FILE in your SHELL to select another file, not inside this file.
#
# LOCAL STORAGE: yarn studio-server:dev:local-storage
# No database/S3 URLs required. Missing shared key and shared local
# credentials are generated/appended once. Private PostgreSQL/MinIO and persistent
# volumes start automatically. Default key-mode login uses the tier KEY or RIVET_KEY.
# Keep generated credentials with the volumes; changing them is not a data reset.
# Old Docker/Kubernetes/file/SQLite data is never adopted automatically.
#
# EXTERNAL STORAGE: yarn studio-server:dev:external-storage
# Set a shared/tier authentication key and the tier's database, bucket, region and
# S3 credentials below. Stores must exist and be reachable INSIDE containers:
# localhost there is not your host. Use a dedicated Rivet database and owned
# workflow prefix; grant permissions for schema migrations, restore table resets
# and S3 read/write/list/delete. External mode never starts local stores as fallback.
# Generate a NEW key if needed (do not replace an existing installation's key):
#   yarn node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# STAGING/PROD: same .env, independent tier values, either storage choice.
#   yarn studio-server:staging:local-storage -- --manifest <candidate.json> --confirm rivet-staging-local
#   yarn studio-server:staging:external-storage -- --manifest <candidate.json> --confirm rivet-staging-external
#   yarn studio-server:prod:local-storage -- --manifest <promoted.json> --confirm rivet-prod-local
#   yarn studio-server:prod:external-storage -- --manifest <promoted.json> --confirm rivet-prod-external
# Staging requires candidate/promoted release evidence and a matching clean
# checkout. Prod additionally requires promoted evidence and predecessor lineage.
# --confirm must match the effective Compose project name; these are CLI flags,
# not .env settings. Local storage does not exempt production from release gates.
#
# Only the proxy is exposed, on 127.0.0.1: dev 8080, staging 8082, prod 8083
# when RIVET_PORT is unset. Set RIVET_PORT to override ALL six commands; two
# installations cannot share the same host port. Tier-specific *_PORT is ignored.
# Internal API, executor, PostgreSQL and MinIO ports are private. A trusted external
# TLS gateway must own public HTTPS; old TLS/tunnel settings are not consumed.
# Stop without deleting data: yarn studio-server:dev:local-storage -- --stop
#
# This file is NOT a blanket container env_file. Only normalized connection,
# identity and UI-auth settings below reach containers. UI auth defaults to key.
# Workflow/provider env values belong in Settings -> Environment variables.
# Settings -> Storage -> Restore legacy backup restores supported v1 archives,
# preserving deployment connections and access. Keep the source encryption key.
# Details: developer-docs/studio-server/server-stack.md.

# COMMON CONFIGURATION
# Shared browser port for every tier/storage choice (optional; defaults above):
# RIVET_PORT=8081
# key or oauth; no unauthenticated mode. For a fresh install start with key,
# save provider settings in Settings -> OAuth and allowed administrator emails
# in Settings -> Server UI access, then set oauth and restart the same installation.
# OAuth with missing settings/empty allowlist denies access; it never falls back
# to key. The authentication key remains required for internal proxy trust.
# Development-auth bypass variables are not forwarded by these launchers.
# RIVET_SERVER_UI_AUTH_MODE=key
# Authentication key >=32 characters: generated if missing in local mode;
# set explicitly in external mode (or use the selected tier's KEY instead).
# RIVET_KEY=replace-with-a-random-authentication-key-at-least-32-characters
# Optional dedicated settings key; otherwise the selected authentication key.
# Backups deliberately exclude keys. Keep the original for encrypted settings.
# RIVET_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-a-private-settings-key
# Previous decryption key, not a request to rotate the primary key:
# RIVET_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS=replace-with-the-previous-settings-key

# LOCAL STORAGE CREDENTIALS (shared by dev, staging and prod)
# Leave unset to generate once. MinIO ID >=3 / secret >=8 characters.
# These are credentials only: each tier still has its own containers/volumes.
# Keep them unchanged with retained volumes. Old tier-prefixed credentials are
# copied to these names on startup only when their values agree; conflicting
# legacy tiers require explicit shared values or separate RIVET_ENV_FILE files.
# RIVET_LOCAL_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-private-postgres-password
# RIVET_LOCAL_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=rivet
# RIVET_LOCAL_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-a-private-minio-secret

# DEVELOPMENT
# Optional tier keys override shared keys:
# RIVET_DEV_KEY=replace-with-a-random-dev-auth-key-at-least-32-characters
# RIVET_DEV_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-a-private-dev-settings-key
# RIVET_DEV_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS=replace-with-the-previous-dev-settings-key
# Leave COMPOSE_PROJECT unset normally: defaults rivet-dev-local/rivet-dev-external.
# A custom name must be unique and stable; do not reuse it between storage choices.
# RIVET_DEV_COMPOSE_PROJECT=my-rivet-dev
# External only: URL-encode special characters in the URL username/password.
# RIVET_DEV_DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://rivet:replace-with-password@dev-db.example:5432/rivet_dev
# verify-full checks the server certificate (recommended with a trusted cert);
# require encrypts without certificate validation and is the launcher default;
# disable is only for an explicitly trusted non-TLS setup. SSL_MODE is authoritative;
# do not embed sslmode/sslcert/sslkey/sslrootcert in the database URL.
# RIVET_DEV_DATABASE_SSL_MODE=verify-full
# AWS: leave ENDPOINT unset for regional S3. MinIO/compatible service: HTTP(S)
# origin only, no bucket/path/query/URL credentials; normally use path-style=true.
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=https://s3.dev.example
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_BUCKET=rivet-dev
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_REGION=us-east-1
# Prefix default workflows/; must end in /, not start with / or contain .. or
# backslashes. runtime-libraries/ is reserved; runtime archives have their own scope.
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_PREFIX=workflows/
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=replace-with-dev-s3-access-key-id
# RIVET_DEV_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-dev-s3-secret-access-key

# STAGING (no fallback to dev/prod credentials; same rules as development)
# RIVET_STAGING_KEY=replace-with-a-random-staging-auth-key-at-least-32-characters
# RIVET_STAGING_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-a-private-staging-settings-key
# RIVET_STAGING_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS=replace-with-the-previous-staging-settings-key
# Default projects: rivet-staging-local/rivet-staging-external.
# RIVET_STAGING_COMPOSE_PROJECT=my-rivet-staging
# External only:
# RIVET_STAGING_DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://rivet:replace-with-password@staging-db.example:5432/rivet_staging
# RIVET_STAGING_DATABASE_SSL_MODE=verify-full
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=https://s3.staging.example
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_BUCKET=rivet-staging
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_REGION=us-east-1
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_PREFIX=workflows/
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=replace-with-staging-s3-access-key-id
# RIVET_STAGING_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-staging-s3-secret-access-key

# PRODUCTION (separate database and installation identity)
# RIVET_PROD_KEY=replace-with-a-random-prod-auth-key-at-least-32-characters
# RIVET_PROD_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-a-private-prod-settings-key
# RIVET_PROD_APP_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS=replace-with-the-previous-prod-settings-key
# Default projects: rivet-prod-local/rivet-prod-external.
# RIVET_PROD_COMPOSE_PROJECT=my-rivet-prod
# External only; AWS example leaves endpoint unset:
# RIVET_PROD_DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://rivet:replace-with-password@prod-db.example:5432/rivet_prod
# RIVET_PROD_DATABASE_SSL_MODE=verify-full
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_BUCKET=rivet-prod
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_REGION=us-east-1
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_PREFIX=workflows/
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=false
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=replace-with-prod-s3-access-key-id
# RIVET_PROD_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-prod-s3-secret-access-key
#
# Existing RIVET_K8S_* external connection values are a PROD compatibility fallback
# only. New Docker installations should use RIVET_PROD_* above.
# Legacy RIVET_VM_K8S_*, VITE_*, PORT, RIVET_API_PORT, tier-specific *_PORT,
# RIVET_ARTIFACTS_HOST_PATH and development-auth/forwarded-header/TLS/tunnel/build
# settings do not configure these six commands. Keep old private credentials
# until older installations/backups are verified; do not copy them into new setup.
